.TH MYSTRCPY 3 "September 2026" "OS Assignment" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mystrcpy \- copy a string to a destination buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.PP
.BI "int mystrcpy(char *" dest ", const char *" src ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mystrcpy
function copies the string pointed to by
.I src
into the buffer pointed to by
.IR dest .
The destination buffer must have enough space to store the source string,
including the terminating null character.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of characters copied.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mystrlen (3),
.BR mystrncpy (3),
.BR mystrcat (3)
